    "question": {
      ":question/id": "22a7b7d6-7758-51dc-8db0-74e352378d2d",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/repairs/2026-10-19-checkbox-nonempty/patched-samples/17592186054676/assets/950531f5fec3c38415dcb83262eb2deda489b73d38dd28752757486e2193841d.png)\n\nIdentify the points that lie on the line $y=2x+4$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(4,9)$, $B(-1,-1)$, $C(2,8)$.\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(4,9)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= 2x+4 \\\\ (9) &= 2(4)+4 \\\\ 9 &= 12 && \\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(-1,-1)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= 2x+4 \\\\ (-1) &= 2(-1)+4 \\\\ -1 &= 2 && \\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(2,8)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= 2x+4 \\\\ (8) &= 2(2)+4 \\\\ 8 &= 8 && \\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only point $C$ lies on the line.",
