      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/repairs/2026-10-19-checkbox-nonempty/patched-samples/17592186054676/assets/ed254cf66863c1021a7c478b50a055f030c3fd56cd5689afe0623f542fee9d17.png)\n\nIdentify the points that lie on the line $y=x+5$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(3,8)$, $B(-2,0)$, $C(1,9)$.\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(3,8)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= x+5 \\\\ (8) &= (3)+5 \\\\ 8 &= 8 && \\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(-2,0)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= x+5 \\\\ (0) &= (-2)+5 \\\\ 0 &= 3 && \\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(1,9)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= x+5 \\\\ (9) &= (1)+5 \\\\ 9 &= 6 && \\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does not lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only point $A$ lies on the line.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "175cdc80-981d-5316-8a0b-b0f5b2149dfa",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "0869481c-97f0-5dfa-a1ee-fedbae66c5c7",
