      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/repairs/2026-10-19-checkbox-nonempty/patched-samples/17592186054676/assets/bfa33f52da6100f8edd066ff95f8ccbd99b1ef2681d9c5da754673373d71f694.png)\n\nIdentify the points that lie on the line $y=3x$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(1,1)$, $B(2,4)$, $C(-3,-9)$.\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(1,1)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= 3x \\\\ (1) &= 3(1) \\\\ 1 &= 3 && \\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(2,4)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= 3x \\\\ (4) &= 3(2) \\\\ 4 &= 6 && \\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(-3,-9)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= 3x \\\\ (-9) &= 3(-3) \\\\ -9 &= -9 && \\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only point $C$ lies on the line.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "8e7e049b-9ba8-557e-bda0-fbe26c4e8680",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "6ab73fa3-6c7e-5c75-860b-9591c09f9249",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "$A$ and $C$ only"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "e1e770cc-b3a1-5782-b0ae-fe5062f360ed",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "$B$ and $C$ only"
            },
