  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186054676,
      "id": "3123f8ed-a1ca-52b7-8427-2f3b60d9e68a",
      "title": "Identifying Points That Lie on a Line"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "f2abacd7-0dc4-5847-9fb1-627cc3967c25",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/repairs/2026-10-19-checkbox-nonempty/patched-samples/17592186054676/assets/802cf242b1d70216b76c5028783a7d19064ad446ca7fa6fc0e12f49a2192014d.png)\n\nIdentify the points that lie on the line $y=2x-1$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(-2,-5)$, $B(3,6)$, $C(2,1)$.\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(-2,-5)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= 2x-1 \\\\ (-5) &= 2(-2)-1 \\\\ -5 &= -5 && \\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(3,6)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= 2x-1 \\\\ (6) &= 2(3)-1 \\\\ 6 &= 5 && \\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(2,1)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= 2x-1 \\\\ (1) &= 2(2)-1 \\\\ 1 &= 3 && \\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does not lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only point $A$ lies on the line.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "35ade46e-5e3d-55d6-8816-a62c8cdc9cb4",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
