    "question": {
      ":question/id": "9d94275a-a341-5f50-a680-81f7a493d685",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/repairs/2026-10-19-checkbox-nonempty/patched-samples/17592186054676/assets/af8ef653967dc019a8ff8826a4ab84d21faa0b002c37fbee864ff6f8d3847c2a.png)\n\nIdentify the points that lie on the line $y=x+5$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(-1,4)$, $B(0,6)$, $C(-4,2)$.\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(-1,4)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= x+5 \\\\ (4) &= (-1)+5 \\\\ 4 &= 4 && \\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(0,6)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= x+5 \\\\ (6) &= (0)+5 \\\\ 6 &= 5 && \\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(-4,2)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= x+5 \\\\ (2) &= (-4)+5 \\\\ 2 &= 1 && \\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does not lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only point $A$ lies on the line.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "36cf3b97-ebc7-53e0-ba6c-aa4f0bf8f99b",
