      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/repairs/2026-10-19-checkbox-nonempty/patched-samples/17592186054676/assets/3151cbcb4bf19dd77a6c51b676c9fe9ac424bcf64ae7e353bd32e484821af7b1.png)\n\nIdentify the points that lie on the line $y=x+1$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(4,5)$, $B(1,-1)$, $C(2,5)$.\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(4,5)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= x+1 \\\\ (5) &= (4)+1 \\\\ 5 &= 5 && \\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(1,-1)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= x+1 \\\\ (-1) &= (1)+1 \\\\ -1 &= 2 && \\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(2,5)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= x+1 \\\\ (5) &= (2)+1 \\\\ 5 &= 3 && \\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does not lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only point $A$ lies on the line.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "9f19f698-a856-50eb-9293-a630b817b91e",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "902147a1-e2f8-5257-b2f5-22824ab8b904",
