      ":question/worked-solution": "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(-3,0)$, $B(-4,-4)$, $C(0,0)$.\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(-3,0)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= x \\\\ (0) &= (-3) \\\\ 0 &= -3 && \\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(-4,-4)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= x \\\\ (-4) &= (-4) \\\\ -4 &= -4 && \\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(0,0)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= x \\\\ (0) &= (0) \\\\ 0 &= 0 && \\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only points $B$ and $C$ lie on the line.",
