      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/repairs/2026-10-19-checkbox-nonempty/patched-samples/17592186054676/assets/a9be14183deb064a51e9f2a614e6b169d7d26ddee2771e58f1aa0b56665b3c91.png)\n\nIdentify the points that lie on the line $y=x+5$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(4,8)$, $B(-4,1)$, $C(1,6)$.\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(4,8)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= x+5 \\\\ (8) &= (4)+5 \\\\ 8 &= 9 && \\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(-4,1)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= x+5 \\\\ (1) &= (-4)+5 \\\\ 1 &= 1 && \\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(1,6)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= x+5 \\\\ (6) &= (1)+5 \\\\ 6 &= 6 && \\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only points $B$ and $C$ lie on the line.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "a3fbfd6f-0ed3-5f98-99d0-f921b49ac927",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
