      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/repairs/2026-10-19-checkbox-nonempty/patched-samples/17592186054676/assets/f1782e4a2520f48f6dd059d6511ece6039b38c261450db63ec90b736587559d9.png)\n\nIdentify the points that lie on the line $y=x+5$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(-2,2)$, $B(1,9)$, $C(4,9)$.\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(-2,2)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= x+5 \\\\ (2) &= (-2)+5 \\\\ 2 &= 3 && \\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(1,9)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= x+5 \\\\ (9) &= (1)+5 \\\\ 9 &= 6 && \\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(4,9)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= x+5 \\\\ (9) &= (4)+5 \\\\ 9 &= 9 && \\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only point $C$ lies on the line.",
