      ":question/worked-solution": "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(0,4)$, $B(1,7)$, $C(3,6)$.\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(0,4)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= x+6 \\\\ (4) &= (0)+6 \\\\ 4 &= 6 && \\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(1,7)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= x+6 \\\\ (7) &= (1)+6 \\\\ 7 &= 7 && \\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(3,6)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= x+6 \\\\ (6) &= (3)+6 \\\\ 6 &= 9 && \\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does not lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only point $B$ lies on the line.",
